the 2022 golden globe awards are without  a network  and tom cruise is returning his trophies  all in response to the ongoing lack of  diversity controversy  with the hollywood foreign press  association here's what we know  i'm always kind of surprised with this  stuff you never know when it's going to  happen  on monday e.t confirmed that tom cruise  sent back his golden globe awards to the  hfpa  amid the continued backlash the  organization faces for its lack of  diversity  an issue that overclouded the show  earlier this year  and just hours later nbc announced plans  to break their long-standing  relationship with the hfpa  and the network will not be airing next  year's golden globes broadcast  nbc said in a statement quote we  continue to believe that the hfpa  is committed to meaningful reform  however change of this magnitude takes  time and work  and we feel strongly that the hfpa needs  time to do it right  as such nbc will not air the 2022  golden globes so what happens now  while the golden globes won't be on nbc  next award season  the ceremony could find a home on  another network or streaming service  but they run the risk of facing an empty  ballroom if the stars continue speaking  out  in february this viral image from the  time's up organization  highlighted the lack of diversity among  the hfpa  which is made up of journalists around  the world in response to a report from  the los  angeles times which first brought  awareness to the hfpa having  zero black journalists in their ranks  the organization said in a statement  quote  we understand that we need to bring in  black members as well as members from  other underrepresented backgrounds  and we will immediately work to  implement an action plan to achieve  these goals as soon as possible the  graphic was shared by stars like  sterling k  brown mark ruffalo and ava duvernay who  wrote on twitter  old news new energy hashtag time's up  globes  additionally scarlett johansson revealed  in a statement that she's often faced  quote  sexist questions and remarks by certain  hfpa members  that bordered on sexual harassment on  monday  et obtained a statement on behalf of the  board members of the hfpa which includes  a commitment to  systemic reform that is long overdue  quote  regardless of the next air date of the  golden globes implementing  transformational changes as quickly  and as thoughtfully as possible remains  the top priority for our organization  they also released an outline of their  course of action from now  until august focused on achieving reform  milestones  looking further into the ceremony's  future nbc  didn't say they're opposed to picking up  the broadcast again  pending the hfpa's response their  statement on monday also  said quote assuming the organization  executes on its plan  we are hopeful we will be in a position  to air the show in january 2023
 

